   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Hello,<br><br>I would like to avoid data discretization as my data is continuous<br><br><img src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/stan-users/attach/4aa6b65e9b531/Auto%20Generated%20Inline%20Image%201?part=0.1\" alt=\"\" height=\"267\" width=\"400\"><br><br>I am fitting this quadratic regression (mode of a gamma function) with a dynamic prior (gamma) which parameters depend of the &quot;x&quot; (I am doing this for a bigger purpose, so consider that I cannot avoid it). Same thing would be valid <br><br>Now, the only stable way I managed to do it, is to discretize the data as you can see, and determine in each partition the mode, which 26 red points are linked by a quadratic function.<br><br>something like<br><br><span style=\"color:#000\"></span><br><span style=\"color:#000\"></span><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">N</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">P</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>transformed parameters</span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">P</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> a</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">P</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> b</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"></span><br><span style=\"color:#000\"><code><span style=\"color:#000\">  vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">P</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span></code></span><code><span style=\"color:#000\">red_dots_mode</span></code><span style=\"color:#000\"><code><span style=\"color:#000\"><code><span style=\"color:#660\"></span></code></span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span></code>  a </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x_partition</span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> alpha_1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> x_partition</span><span style=\"color:#660\">^</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> alpha_2 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> alpha_3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  b </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x_partition</span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> beta_1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> x_partition</span><span style=\"color:#660\">^</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> beta_2 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> beta_3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>  red_dots_mode </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">a</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">b<br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>model</span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>   </span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">p </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">PARTITIONS</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">p</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> gamma</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">a</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">p</span><span style=\"color:#660\">],</span><span style=\"color:#000\">b</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">p</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br></span></div></code></div><br><br>Is it possible to not partition since the infinite loss functions are all linked quadratically. &quot;x&quot; being continuous instead of discrete.<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#000\"><code><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>model</span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>   </span><span style=\"color:#000\">y</span><span style=\"color:#660\"></span><span style=\"color:#000\"></span><span style=\"color:#660\"></span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> gamma</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\"></span></code></span><span style=\"color:#000\"><code><span style=\"color:#000\"><code><span style=\"color:#000\"><code><span style=\"color:#000\">x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> alpha_1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> x^2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> alpha_2 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> alpha_3</span></code></span></code></span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"></span></code></span><span style=\"color:#000\"><code><span style=\"color:#000\"><code><span style=\"color:#000\"><code><span style=\"color:#000\">x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> beta_1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> x^2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> beta_2 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> beta_3</span></code></span></code></span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></code><br> </span></div></code></div><br><br>I hope is not too confusing!<br>Thanks<br>"
    ]
   ]
