     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I respond in line</div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><br>On Saturday, July 23, 2016 at 2:37:11 AM UTC+10, Bob Carpenter wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">Did you just want to fit all the data to the likelihood?\r\n<br>\r\n<br>&gt; y ~ gamma(x* alpha_1 + x^2* alpha_2 + alpha_3,x* beta_1 + x^2* beta_2 + beta_3);\r\n<br>\r\n<br>If so, what went wrong?  \r\n<br></blockquote><div><br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>This is convergence for <b>discretized </b>(decent)</div><div><br></div><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-gdoIqiZoVjg/V5K_jA-f7iI/AAAAAAAAEj4/59uDXw02ousQaXxNG2X-d5jJT1ept3mbQCLcB/s1600/Capture88.PNG\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-gdoIqiZoVjg/V5K_jA-f7iI/AAAAAAAAEj4/59uDXw02ousQaXxNG2X-d5jJT1ept3mbQCLcB/s1600/Capture88.PNG&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792460731944000&amp;usg=AOvVaw12xDhu8aLru-hv6yERTTdZ\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-gdoIqiZoVjg/V5K_jA-f7iI/AAAAAAAAEj4/59uDXw02ousQaXxNG2X-d5jJT1ept3mbQCLcB/s320/Capture88.PNG\" border=\"0\" width=\"320\" height=\"192\"></a></p><div><br></div><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"></p><div><br></div><div>This is non-convergence for <b>NON </b>discretized (failed)<br></div><div> </div><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-vDeVSdIDsFU/V5Mg2RQXEgI/AAAAAAAAEkI/1ALaLXY8xswu6KIIYjGnDEG4Fcxaxb7CACLcB/s1600/Capture77.PNG\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-vDeVSdIDsFU/V5Mg2RQXEgI/AAAAAAAAEkI/1ALaLXY8xswu6KIIYjGnDEG4Fcxaxb7CACLcB/s1600/Capture77.PNG&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792460731944000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0oBkSG18Ak_mrktyCzNrRh\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-vDeVSdIDsFU/V5Mg2RQXEgI/AAAAAAAAEkI/1ALaLXY8xswu6KIIYjGnDEG4Fcxaxb7CACLcB/s320/Capture77.PNG\" border=\"0\" width=\"320\" height=\"191\"></a></p><div><br></div><div>It seems that with 6 parameters linked in 2 quadratic equations, Stan need discretization to work.</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">\r\n<br>- Bob\r\n<br>\r\n<br>&gt; On Jul 22, 2016, at 3:26 AM, Jan &lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">mangiol...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:\r\n<br>&gt; \r\n<br>&gt; Hello,\r\n<br>&gt; \r\n<br>&gt; I would like to avoid data discretization as my data is continuous\r\n<br>&gt; \r\n<br>&gt; &lt;Auto Generated Inline Image 1.png&gt;\r\n<br>&gt; \r\n<br>&gt; I am fitting this quadratic regression (mode of a gamma function) with a dynamic prior (gamma) which parameters depend of the &quot;x&quot; (I am doing this for a bigger purpose, so consider that I cannot avoid it). Same thing would be valid \r\n<br>&gt; \r\n<br>&gt; Now, the only stable way I managed to do it, is to discretize the data as you can see, and determine in each partition the mode, which 26 red points are linked by a quadratic function.\r\n<br>&gt; \r\n<br>&gt; something like\r\n<br>&gt; \r\n<br>&gt; \r\n<br>&gt; data{\r\n<br>&gt; vector[N] y[P]\r\n<br>&gt; }\r\n<br>&gt; transformed parameters{\r\n<br>&gt;   vector&lt;lower=0&gt;[P] a;\r\n<br>&gt;   vector&lt;lower=0&gt;[P] b;\r\n<br>&gt;   vector&lt;lower=0&gt;[P] red_dots_mode;\r\n<br>&gt; \r\n<br>&gt;   a = (x_partition* alpha_1 + x_partition^2* alpha_2 + alpha_3);\r\n<br>&gt;   b = (x_partition* beta_1 + x_partition^2* beta_2 + beta_3);\r\n<br>&gt; \r\n<br>&gt;   red_dots_mode = (a-1)/b\r\n<br>&gt; }\r\n<br>&gt; model{\r\n<br>&gt;    for(p in 1:PARTITIONS) y[p] ~ gamma(a[p],b[p]);\r\n<br>&gt; } \r\n<br>&gt; \r\n<br>&gt; \r\n<br>&gt; Is it possible to not partition since the infinite loss functions are all linked quadratically. &quot;x&quot; being continuous instead of discrete.\r\n<br>&gt; \r\n<br>&gt; \r\n<br>&gt; \r\n<br>&gt; model{\r\n<br>&gt;    y ~ gamma(x* alpha_1 + x^2* alpha_2 + alpha_3,x* beta_1 + x^2* beta_2 + beta_3);\r\n<br>&gt; } \r\n<br>&gt; \r\n<br>&gt;  \r\n<br>&gt; \r\n<br>&gt; \r\n<br>&gt; I hope is not too confusing!\r\n<br>&gt; Thanks\r\n<br>&gt; \r\n<br>&gt; -- \r\n<br>&gt; You received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;Stan users mailing list&quot; group.\r\n<br>&gt; To unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a rel=\"nofollow\">stan-users+...@googlegroups.com</a>.\r\n<br>&gt; To post to this group, send email to <a rel=\"nofollow\">stan-...@googlegroups.com</a>.\r\n<br>&gt; For more options, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/optout\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/optout&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792460731944000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2jETKQPAgYUgQ-JNgaHbAm\">https://groups.google.com/d/optout</a>.\r\n<br>&gt; &lt;Auto Generated Inline Image 1.png&gt;\r\n<br>\r\n<br></blockquote></div>"
    ]
   ]
