   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Thanks Ben,<div><br></div><div>I will definitely try.  Before I have to fix a stability issue <br><br><a href=\"https://groups.google.com/forum/#!category-topic/stan-users/general/Sc__sjevbbY\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/forum/%23!category-topic/stan-users/general/Sc__sjevbbY&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792460731953000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2a5IrpPLb742RERbnl80JD\">https://groups.google.com/forum/#!category-topic/stan-users/general/Sc__sjevbbY</a><br><br>given by unexpected outcome for variable constraining for positive a and b in gamma(a, b).</div><div><br></div><div>If you could have a look would be great!</div><div>Thanks</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br><br>On Sunday, July 24, 2016 at 12:27:58 AM UTC+10, Ben Goodrich wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">On Saturday, July 23, 2016 at 3:53:51 AM UTC-4, Jan wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Seems\r\n interesting! So it&#39;s kernel statistics and/or qr decomposition. It \r\nsomething that I&#39;m not familiar with so so far i cannot translate such \r\ninfo into my model. I&#39;m reading about it, but if you have some code for \r\ndoing it would be great.</div></blockquote><div> <br>If you use R, then you can just do <br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">X </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> poly</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">predictor</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> degree </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> raw </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>xbar </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> colMeans</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">X</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>X </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sweep</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">X</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> xbar</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>QR </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> qr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">X</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>Q </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> qr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">Q</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">QR</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>R </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> qr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">R</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">QR</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>then pass the two columns of Q to Stan and modify your Stan code to be<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><code><span style=\"color:#000\"><code><span style=\"color:#000\"><span style=\"color:#000\">y</span></span><span style=\"color:#660\"></span><span style=\"color:#000\"></span><span style=\"color:#660\"></span><span style=\"color:#000\"><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span></span><span style=\"color:#660\"><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span></span><span style=\"color:#000\"><span style=\"color:#000\"> gamma</span></span><span style=\"color:#660\"><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span></span><span style=\"color:#000\"></span></code></span><span style=\"color:#000\"><code><span style=\"color:#000\"><code><span style=\"color:#000\"><code><span style=\"color:#000\"><span style=\"color:#000\">q1</span></span><span style=\"color:#660\"><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span></span><span style=\"color:#000\"><span style=\"color:#000\"> alpha_1 </span></span><span style=\"color:#660\"><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span></span><span style=\"color:#000\"><span style=\"color:#000\"> q2 </span></span><span style=\"color:#660\"><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span></span><span style=\"color:#000\"><span style=\"color:#000\"> alpha_2 </span></span><span style=\"color:#660\"><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span></span><span style=\"color:#000\"><span style=\"color:#000\"> alpha_3</span></span></code></span></code></span><span style=\"color:#660\"><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> q1 </span></span></code></span><span style=\"color:#000\"><code><span style=\"color:#000\"><code><span style=\"color:#000\"><code><span style=\"color:#000\"></span><span style=\"color:#660\"><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span></span><span style=\"color:#000\"><span style=\"color:#000\"> beta_1 </span></span><span style=\"color:#660\"><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span></span><span style=\"color:#000\"><span style=\"color:#000\"> q2 </span></span><span style=\"color:#660\"><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span></span><span style=\"color:#000\"><span style=\"color:#000\"> beta_2 </span></span><span style=\"color:#660\"><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span></span><span style=\"color:#000\"><span style=\"color:#000\"> beta_3</span></span></code></span></code></span><span style=\"color:#660\"><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span></span><span style=\"color:#000\"><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></span></code></span></code></div></code></div><br>To interpret the coefficients in terms of X, you have to pre-multiply them by the inverse of R.<br><br>Ben<br><br></div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
