an><span style=\"color:#660\"><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span></span><span style=\"color:#000\"><span style=\"color:#000\"> beta_2 </span></span><span style=\"color:#660\"><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span></span><span style=\"color:#000\"><span style=\"color:#000\"> beta_3</span></span></code></span></code></span><span style=\"color:#660\"><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span></span><span style=\"color:#000\"><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></span></code></span></code></div></code></div><br>To interpret the coefficients in terms of X, you have to pre-multiply them by the inverse of R.<br><br>Ben<br><br></div></div></blockquote></div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
